//============================================================================
// nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads --- Calibre BOND PAD (BND) wrapper deck  (PROJECT-OWNED)
//
// Run it with:   DRC_GDS=/abs/path.gds scripts/calibre/run_bnd.sh
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
// --------------------
// The Europractice mini@sic manual requires the final GDS to be "DRC/ANT/BND
// clean". BND is the wire-bond pad rule set and it has never been run on this
// design.
//
// WHICH FOUNDRY DECK: this file does not name one. $BND_FOUNDRY_DECK is resolved
// per site from $(TSMC_65_HOME) by ASIC/genus-innovus/drc_project.mk, which is
// gitignored. It must select the WIRE BOND deck for the SAME metal stack as the
// DRC deck and as the Innovus GdsOutMap used by write_stream -- a mismatched
// stack is a silently-wrong result, not an error. The deck's release name
// encodes a metal stack and a purchased revision, so it is site configuration,
// not source. See ci/site.env.example.
//
// Same placeholder problem as the DRC and ANT decks -- the shipped deck's layout
// path, primary cell, results database and summary report are literal
// placeholder strings the customer is expected to replace -- so the same
// `DRC ICSTATION YES` wrapper pattern applies. The deck's own text is not
// reproduced here: this repository is public and TSMC's licence does not permit
// it. Read the block in your own PDK.
//
// THE PITCH OPTION IS MANDATORY AND WE WERE NOT SETTING IT
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MEASURED 2026-08-09 run (calibre_runs/bnd_run_20260809): 197 rulechecks
// executed, only TWO non-zero -- and one of them was the deck telling us it was
// misconfigured, via its own PITCH_OPTION.ERROR.1 rulecheck, which fires when no
// pitch option has been selected. With no pitch option defined the deck falls
// through to its final #ELSE and sets every pad-row layer it derives to EMPTY.
// Every pad-row-derived check then evaluates against nothing. THE ~200 ZEROS
// WERE A FABRICATED CLEAN, not a pass.
//
// PITCH_70_STAGGER is the right one, on two independent pieces of evidence:
//   - we instantiate PAD70GU and PAD70NU (place_bondpads.tcl:140-165), i.e.
//     70um-pitch bond pads; the library's single-in-line variants PAD70GU_SL /
//     PAD70NU_SL are NOT used.
//   - floorplan.tcl:11 -- the bond ring is staggered, PAD70GU outer and PAD70NU
//     inner. Two rows = staggered, not single-in-line.
#DEFINE PITCH_70_STAGGER
//
// CORRECTION to what this file used to claim: it said a single-pad switch was
// "a switch left at the foundry default". That was wrong. The lines it cited are
// inside the BODIES of single-pitch #IFDEF blocks that never execute; that name
// is not a top-level switch, and single-pad is the wrong structure for us anyway.
//
//   The after-passivation redistribution-metal switch is active in the shipped
//   deck, and that is correct for us: our stack carries AlRDL and the design has
//   AP geometry. Change it HERE, never in the read-only PDK.
// If the broker's own switch set differs, theirs wins: ask before overriding.
//
// EXPECT NOISE ON THIS ONE, AND KNOW WHY
// --------------------------------------
// Bond pads (tpbn65v PAD70NU/PAD70GU) stream as near-empty black boxes -- a
// handful of polygons each, on a few layers -- and the passivation-opening layer
// does not appear ANYWHERE in the stream. A bond-pad deck with no pad openings
// cannot evaluate pad-opening rules, so those will be silent rather than clean.
// The useful signal tonight is the metal/AP geometry around the pad ring, not
// the pad openings themselves. Treat a green pad-opening result as absence of
// evidence, exactly as with the corner CSR checks.
//
// The foundry deck is READ-ONLY and is not copied, patched or sed-ed.
//============================================================================

DRC ICSTATION YES

LAYOUT PATH    "$DRC_GDS"
LAYOUT SYSTEM  GDSII
LAYOUT PRIMARY "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads"

DRC RESULTS DATABASE "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.bnd.results" ASCII
DRC SUMMARY REPORT   "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.bnd.summary" REPLACE HIER
DRC CELL NAME YES CELL SPACE XFORM

DRC MAXIMUM RESULTS 1000
DRC MAXIMUM VERTEX  4096

#DEFINE LP

INCLUDE "$BND_FOUNDRY_DECK"
